Let the cost of each philosophy book be $P$.
Benjamin bought 2 copies of a philosophy book at $45 each, so the cost of the philosophy books is $2 \times 45 = 90$.

The total cost of his purchases is the sum of the costs of the sci-fi novels, history books, and philosophy books.
